# Configuration for the daily automated run.
#
# Copy to the project root as `monitor.env`, fill in, then:  chmod 600 monitor.env
# Never commit this file. Never put secrets in a crontab.

# --- Where the dashboard is published -------------------------------------
# A mapped SharePoint library, a synced OneDrive folder, or any file share the
# policy directorate can already open. No new permissions to grant.
MONITOR_PUBLISH_TO="/mnt/sharepoint/policy/senedd-monitor/index.html"
# The same location as a URL, so the digest email can link to it.
MONITOR_DASHBOARD_URL="https://nrla.sharepoint.com/sites/policy/senedd-monitor/index.html"

# --- Email ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing is sent unless MONITOR_SMTP_HOST is set. That is deliberate: a
# half-configured install cannot email a distribution list by accident.
MONITOR_FROM="joshua.helm-cowley@nrla.org.uk"
MONITOR_TO="policy@nrla.org.uk,joshua.helm-cowley@nrla.org.uk"
MONITOR_SMTP_HOST="smtp.office365.com"
MONITOR_SMTP_PORT="587"
MONITOR_SMTP_USER="joshua.helm-cowley@nrla.org.uk"
MONITOR_SMTP_PASS=""

# --- Welsh Government content ---------------------------------------------
# Three routes; see SPECIFICATION.md section 4.5 and WELSH-GOVERNMENT-SETUP.md.
#
# The newsroom at media.service.gov.wales runs on every run, everywhere, and
# needs no configuration whatever. There is no switch for it because there is
# no deployment in which turning it off is the right answer. It carries Welsh
# Government announcements — but NOT the consultation register.
#
# On NRLA infrastructure, gov.wales is reachable directly, so leave the route
# as "rss" and a failure is then a REAL failure worth flagging.
MONITOR_GOVWALES_ROUTE="rss"
#
# On any cloud host, gov.wales returns 403 whatever you send. Set the route to
# "mailbox" and configure the mailbox below, otherwise the RSS source is
# reported as broken on every single run and people stop reading the banner.
# MONITOR_GOVWALES_ROUTE="mailbox"
#
# The mailbox route closes the consultation-register gap. Four values, from the
# Entra ID app registration IT create for you. The client SECRET is the value
# shown once at creation — not the Secret ID, which is not a password.
# MONITOR_MAILBOX="joshua.helm-cowley@nrla.org.uk"
# MONITOR_GRAPH_TENANT=""
# MONITOR_GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=""
# MONITOR_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#
# MONITOR_GRAPH_TOKEN is a pasted Graph access token. It lasts about an hour,
# so it is useful for one manual test and nothing else — and it OVERRIDES the
# four values above, so leave it unset unless you are doing exactly that test.
# MONITOR_GRAPH_TOKEN=""

# --- Tuning ---------------------------------------------------------------
# How far back each run looks. 21 days comfortably covers a fortnight's
# publishing lag plus a bank holiday. Deduplication means overlap is free.
MONITOR_LOOKBACK_DAYS="21"
